# QRDX release maintainers — who may sign a release (docs/RELEASES.md).
#
# One line per maintainer key, in OpenSSH allowed-signers format, restricted to the two
# namespaces a maintainer signs in — "git" (the release TAG, checked by the release workflow
# with `git verify-tag`) and "qrdx-release" (the release MANIFEST):
#
#   alice@qrdx.org namespaces="git,qrdx-release" sk-ssh-ed25519@openssh.com AAAAGnNr...
#
# (The namespace is part of what is signed, so neither signature can stand in for the other.)
# Prefer hardware-backed keys (sk-ssh-ed25519@openssh.com, e.g. a YubiKey).
#
# A release verifies only when at least `maintainer_threshold` (release/policy.json) distinct
# maintainers listed here have signed its manifest, AND (unless skipped) the release workflow's
# own Sigstore signature checks out. Changes to this file are themselves a release-trust change:
# land them through review, signed by existing maintainers, and announce them out of band.
#
# EMPTY ON PURPOSE: no maintainer keys are registered yet, so nothing verifies until they are.
